  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t)-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t).$ At time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ the particle is located at the position $x=5.$ \nFind the position of the particle at time $t=\\pi .$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "The position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is equal to its position at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\pi )=x(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\pi ) & =5+{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t)-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =5+{[\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t)+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t)]}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =5+[\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi )]-[\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =5+(0-1)-(1+0) \\\\  & =5-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is $x=3.$",
